      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلْقَصَّارِ يُسَلَّمُ إِلَيْهِ اَلْمَتَاعُ فَيُحْرِقُهُ أَوْ يَخْرِقُهُ أَ يُغَرَّمُهُ قَالَ \"نَعَمْ غُرِّمَهُ بِمَا جَنَتْ يَدُهُ فَإِنَّكَ إِنَّمَا أَعْطَيْتَهُ لِيُصْلِحَ وَ لَمْ تُعْطِهِ لِيُفْسِدَ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3918 - Ali bin Al-Hakam narrated from Isma'il bin Al-Sabbah, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdillah (as) about a launderer to whom a garment is given, but he burns or tears it. Should he be held liable?\nImam (as) said: \"Yes, he is liable for the damage caused by his actions, for you gave it to him to repair or clean, not to ruin.\""
        ]
      }
